[36m(TaskRunner pid=223690)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=223690)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=223690)[0m d \equiv 1 \pmod{10}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=223690)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=223690)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=223690)[0m But note: any number divisible by 5 can only end in 0 or 5. Therefore, any divisor of $9!$ divisible by 5 cannot have a units digit of 1. Thus, such divisors must not include the factor 5. That is, we can focus on the part of the factorization that excludes 5:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=223690)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=223690)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=223690)[0m \text{Allowed divisors are of the form } 2^a \cdot 3^b \cdot 7^c
[36m(TaskRunner pid=223690)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=223690)[0m where $0 \leq a \leq 7$, $0 \leq b \leq 4$, $0 \leq c \leq 1$.
